# DISABLED EXAMPLE. Rename to 46-customer-portal.caddy inside the gateway's
# /etc/caddy/routes.d/ to turn the customer portal on.
#
# The customer portal (backend-rs/src/routes/customer_portal.rs) is NEW in Rust:
# there is no Python implementation of any of these routes, so, unlike every
# other group in this directory, there is NO failover to `api:8010`. With the
# Rust container down these paths answer the gateway's 502, and the customer
# sees the portal page's "try again later" state; nothing else in the product is
# affected. Moving this file to `routes.d/off/` switches the feature off (Python
# answers 404 {"detail":"Not Found"}, which the page shows as an invalid link).
#
# One matcher covers the whole group:
#   /api/v1/customer-portal/links...   tenant management (a person's JWT; never
#                                      an API key: the route is Internal)
#   /api/v1/customer-portal/customers  customers that have commitments
#   /api/v1/customer-portal/public/... the two token routes a customer calls
#                                      with no login (read the page, answer)
#
# Public routes need nothing from the gateway for security: the link's token is
# the credential, every bad link is one identical 404, rate limits run in the
# service per address and per link, and the responses carry Cache-Control:
# no-store, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and X-Robots-Tag: noindex. The gateway
# must forward X-Forwarded-For (Caddy's reverse_proxy does by default) because
# the per-address limit reads the first hop.

@rs_customer_portal {
	path /api/v1/customer-portal/*
}
handle @rs_customer_portal {
	reverse_proxy api-rs:8021 {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 5s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
